+# HIL Ingest & Audit Runbook
+
+Purpose
+- Ensure HIL and sim artifacts are treated as first-class datasets with schema, provenance, and versioning.
+- Ingest artifacts into MLflow and OpenLineage; record evidence manifests and sign artifacts for auditors.
+
+Steps
+1. Register sensor schema:
+   python ops/data/schema_registry/register_schema.py --name sensor.trace --version 1 ops/data/schemas/sensor_schema_v1.json
+
+2. Run HIL campaign (operator-run) and collect artifacts under a directory (e.g., /data/hil/CAMPAIGN123).
+
+3. Validate & ingest traces:
+   python ops/data/ingest/validate_and_ingest.py --file /data/hil/CAMPAIGN123/capture.ndjson --schema ops/data/schemas/sensor_schema_v1.json --capture-id CAMPAIGN123 --mlflow-uri http://mlflow:5000 --s3-uri s3://aegis-hil/
+
+4. Ingest HIL artifacts (logs, video, debug) as a campaign:
+   python ops/hil/ingest_hil_artifacts.py --campaign-id CAMPAIGN123 --artifact-dir /data/hil/CAMPAIGN123
+
+5. Package formal artifacts and sign:
+   COSIGN_KMS_URI=awskms://... ./ops/formal/package_and_sign_formal.sh /tmp/aegis_formal_bundle
+
+6. Produce auditor bundle:
+   ./ops/ci/prepare_auditor_bundle.sh /tmp/aegis_hil_audit.tar.gz
+
+Notes:
+- Ensure MLflow, OpenLineage (Marquez), and S3 backends are configured and reachable from the ingest host.
+- Evidence manifests are recorded to link each action to a Rekor/cosign entry where applicable.
+
